# An OpenTheory article (format version 6, https://www.gilith.com/opentheory/article.html)
# that the reader must reject. It is accepted_choice_commutativity_instance.art beside it,
# whose header explains the encoding, up to the last block: the proof derives
#   |- choice (choice x y) y = choice y (choice x y)
# and thm claims
#   |- choice (choice x y) y = y
# instead. The claim would also equate every term with the empty choice: with y the empty
# choice, the commutativity of the choice and its unit law, empty + M = M, turn it into
# x = the empty choice.
